# Camera & Controller Reference: XP Hero

Primary feel reference for planet locomotion and follow camera.

- Gameplay video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9mEIWC1gjDo
- Still: `docs/refs/xp-hero-camera-controller.png`
- Art is placeholder; match **feel**, not visuals. Ground is **spherical** — adapt XP Hero’s flat-world camera to radial up.

## Target feel (XP Hero)

- High-angle follow (top-down-ish tilt), not over-the-shoulder.
- **Fixed viewing compass**: camera yaw does **not** spin with character facing.
- Character rotates to face move direction; camera stays put.
- Virtual joystick / WASD: move relative to **camera view** on the ground plane.
- Soft, stable follow — no terrain bob, no jitter, no sudden angle pops.
- Framing: hero near center (slightly lower), wide readable play space around them.
- Casual mobile survivor/ARPG readability over cinematic drama.

## Spherical adaptations (BackHome)

- Prefer **planet radial up** for camera tilt, never noisy terrain normals.
- Parallel-transport the camera’s view-forward on the sphere (no antipode flip / W↔S invert).
- Damp focus height separately from planar follow so hills don’t shake the camera.
- Do **not** auto-orbit the camera when the player walks “backward” unless explicitly requested — XP Hero keeps a fixed compass.
- Keep `followTargetFacing` off for the default casual XP Hero feel.
- Motion framing: slight zoom-out punch when walk starts, then settle into a more top-down travel pitch + look-ahead so sphere foreshortening stays readable. Idle framing returns softly.

## When changing camera/controls

1. Ask: would this still feel like XP Hero on a curved planet?
2. Prefer stability and readability over “smart” camera turns.
3. Tune offsets toward high angle (more height, moderate back) rather than third-person chase.
